B.Ww=new A.dh(0,16,"Behind these iron gates lies what is often described as the world's first open-air concentration camp.")
B.Wo=new A.dh(16,38,"In 1679, over 1,200 Scottish Covenanters were imprisoned in this muddy field without shelter.")
B.WB=new A.dh(38,62,"For four bitter months, with four ounces of bread a day, many perished from starvation and exposure.")
B.Wn=new A.dh(62,90,"Today, this enclosure stands as a solemn memorial to Scotland's turbulent religious history.")
B.If=s([B.Ww,B.Wo,B.WB,B.Wn],t.M3)
B.Wk=new A.kH("stop-b","Stop B","Covenanters' Prison","Head to the Covenanters' Prison","Walk towards the northern section of the graveyard to find the gated entrance to the Covenanters' Prison.","Stand near the iron gates of the prison. Listen to the tragic story of what took place here in 1679.","assets/audio/covenanters.mp3","",null,B.HU,2,"Behind these iron gates lies what is often described as the world's first open-air concentration camp.\n\nIn 1679, following the Battle of Bothwell Bridge, over 1,200 Scottish Covenanters \u2014 Presbyterians who resisted the King's attempts to enforce Anglican worship \u2014 were marched here and imprisoned in this muddy field.\n\nFor over four bitter months through autumn and winter, with no roof or shelter, they survived on four ounces of bread a day. Many perished from exposure and starvation. Others were executed at the nearby Grassmarket, while over 250 were sentenced to transportation to the Caribbean, only to perish in a shipwreck off Orkney.\n\nToday, this enclosure remains a solemn memorial to their sacrifice.",B.If)
